"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Artificial Intelligence\",\n      \"type\": \"Technology\",\n      \"description\": \"Artificial Intelligence (AI) is a rapidly advancing technology that has the potential to revolutionize various industries and aspects of daily life, but it also presents complex ethical dilemmas and challenges.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Potential Benefits\": \"Improved efficiency and productivity\",\n        \"Potential Harms\": \"Job displacement, inequality, concentration of power, biased outcomes, privacy violations\",\n        \"Complexity\": \"Rapidly advancing, multifaceted, complex and opaque\",\n        \"Autonomy\": \"Increasingly autonomous decision-making capabilities\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"facial recognition technology\",\n      \"type\": \"Technology\",\n      \"description\": \"Facial recognition technology is a method of identifying or verifying the identity of an individual using their face. It can be used for various purposes, including surveillance, security, and access control.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Purpose\": \"Surveillance, Security, Access Control\",\n        \"Ethical Concerns\": \"Right to Privacy, Potential for Abuse of Power\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"adoption\",\n      \"type\": \"Process\",\n      \"description\": \"The process of accepting and integrating AI systems into various aspects of life and industry, which can be influenced by factors such as trust, ethical considerations, and societal implications.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Influencing Factors\": \"Trust, Ethical Considerations, Societal Implications\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"trust\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Trust is a fundamental aspect in the ethical development and deployment of AI technologies, particularly in ensuring that users and stakeholders have confidence in the systems\\\" decisions and processes.\",\n  